{"version":"0.12.24","prev_tag":"v0.12.23","target":"default","tag_prefix":"","area_scope":[],"commits":[{"sha":"280670217b0da8f2a541b655b9965c79124a1660","title":"Unify account auth, remember browser profiles, and retain usage evidence (#1307)","files":["docs/architecture-reference.md","docs/architecture/codebase.md","docs/architecture/data.md","docs/config.md","docs/getting-started.md","docs/lf.md","docs/subscriptions.md","docs/troubleshooting.md","python/tests/test_auth_cron_evidence.py","rust/loopflow/src/bin/lf.rs","rust/loopflow/src/controller/task/mod.rs","rust/loopflow/src/controller/wave/runner.rs","rust/loopflow/src/engine/agent.rs","rust/loopflow/src/engine/builtins.rs","rust/loopflow/src/engine/builtins/ops/skill/init.md","rust/loopflow/src/engine/builtins/ops/skill/loopflow.md","rust/loopflow/src/lf/commands/auth.rs","rust/loopflow/src/lf/commands/auth_input.rs","rust/loopflow/src/lf/commands/auth_status.rs","rust/loopflow/src/lf/commands/profile.rs","rust/loopflow/src/lf/commands/run.rs","rust/loopflow/src/lf/mod.rs","rust/loopflow/src/ops/pm.rs","rust/loopflow/src/ops/pm/oauth_tests.rs","rust/loopflow/src/profile.rs","rust/loopflow/src/provider_account.rs","rust/loopflow/src/provider_account/lease.rs","rust/loopflow/src/provider_auth/browser_handoff.rs","rust/loopflow/src/provider_auth/mod.rs","rust/loopflow/src/run_record.rs","rust/loopflow/src/store/migrations.rs","rust/loopflow/src/store/migrations/drafts/auth_browser_bindings__2cd101ad721f80ca7903d743acc094c4.sql","rust/loopflow/src/store/mod.rs","rust/loopflow/src/store/sqlite.rs","rust/loopflow/src/subscription.rs","rust/loopflow/tests/auth_tests.rs","rust/loopflow/tests/global_commands.rs","rust/loopflow/tests/terminal_control_tests.rs","scripts/bootstrap-cron-host.sh","scripts/demo_profile_routing.py","tests/e2e/linear_oauth.py","tests/fixtures/dto/auth_routes.json","tests/fixtures/dto/auth_status.json","wave/infrastructure/MEMORY.md"]},{"sha":"418e52ba652c4054879da67851f18d23e6b64a62","title":"Keep branch builds on private data and installed Tasks on their owning runtime (#1308)","files":[".github/workflows/ci.yml",".github/workflows/package-build.yml","README.md","TESTING.md","docs/agent-api.md","docs/architecture-reference.md","docs/architecture.html","docs/architecture.md","docs/architecture/codebase.md","docs/architecture/data.md","docs/architecture/delivery.md","docs/architecture/homes.md","docs/architecture/planning.md","docs/authoring.md","docs/conducting.md","docs/getting-started.md","docs/glossary.md","docs/index.md","docs/lf.md","docs/security.md","docs/troubleshooting.md","docs/waves.md","python/tests/test_loopflow_skill_alignment.py","python/tests/test_release_automation.py","release/CRON_HOST.md","rust/loopflow/provider.txt","rust/loopflow/src/bin/lf.rs","rust/loopflow/src/bin/lfd.rs","rust/loopflow/src/controller/task/mod.rs","rust/loopflow/src/controller/wave/README.md","rust/loopflow/src/controller/wave/mod.rs","rust/loopflow/src/controller/wave/runtime.rs","rust/loopflow/src/controller/wave/server.rs","rust/loopflow/src/durable.rs","rust/loopflow/src/engine/builtins.rs","rust/loopflow/src/engine/builtins/LOOPFLOW.md","rust/loopflow/src/engine/builtins/ops/skill/init.md","rust/loopflow/src/engine/builtins/ops/skill/loopflow.md","rust/loopflow/src/engine/builtins/ops/skill/review-chapter.md","rust/loopflow/src/engine/builtins/ops/skill/start-chapter.md","rust/loopflow/src/engine/builtins/task/skill/advance.md","rust/loopflow/src/engine/builtins/task/skill/design.md","rust/loopflow/src/engine/builtins/task/skill/launch-plan.md","rust/loopflow/src/engine/builtins/wave/skill/assess.md","rust/loopflow/src/engine/builtins/wave/skill/s3-scan.md","rust/loopflow/src/engine/builtins/wave/skill/scan.md","rust/loopflow/src/engine/builtins/wave/skill/split-wave.md","rust/loopflow/src/engine/builtins/wave/skill/update-wave.md","rust/loopflow/src/engine/builtins/wave/skill/wave-report.md","rust/loopflow/src/engine/builtins/wave/skill/wave_chat.md","rust/loopflow/src/engine/builtins/wave/skill/wave_operate.md","rust/loopflow/src/engine/builtins/wave/skill/wave_review-chapter.md","rust/loopflow/src/engine/builtins/wave/skill/wave_start-chapter.md","rust/loopflow/src/engine/process.rs","rust/loopflow/src/engine/wave_home.rs","rust/loopflow/src/lf/commands/chat.rs","rust/loopflow/src/lf/commands/home.rs","rust/loopflow/src/lf/commands/install.rs","rust/loopflow/src/lf/commands/install/published.rs","rust/loopflow/src/lf/commands/install/recovery.rs","rust/loopflow/src/lf/commands/mod.rs","rust/loopflow/src/lf/commands/ops/mod.rs","rust/loopflow/src/lf/commands/placement.rs","rust/loopflow/src/lf/commands/runs.rs","rust/loopflow/src/lf/commands/ssh.rs","rust/loopflow/src/lf/commands/wave_intent.rs","rust/loopflow/src/lf/commands/waves.rs","rust/loopflow/src/lf/discovery.rs","rust/loopflow/src/lf/mod.rs","rust/loopflow/src/lfd/mod.rs","rust/loopflow/src/machine_install.rs","rust/loopflow/src/ops/child.rs","rust/loopflow/src/ops/flow.rs","rust/loopflow/src/ops/home.rs","rust/loopflow/src/ops/human_session.rs","rust/loopflow/src/ops/mod.rs","rust/loopflow/src/ops/pm/task_comments_tests.rs","rust/loopflow/src/ops/pm/task_planning_tests.rs","rust/loopflow/src/ops/pr.rs","rust/loopflow/src/ops/project.rs","rust/loopflow/src/ops/task.rs","rust/loopflow/src/ops/task_destination.rs","rust/loopflow/src/ops/task_execution.rs","rust/loopflow/src/ops/task_flow.rs","rust/loopflow/src/run_record.rs","rust/loopflow/src/store/branch_data.rs","rust/loopflow/src/store/durable.rs","rust/loopflow/src/store/migrations.rs","rust/loopflow/src/store/mod.rs","rust/loopflow/src/store/sqlite.rs","rust/loopflow/src/store/sqlite/durable.rs","rust/loopflow/src/wave_host.rs","rust/loopflow/src/work/task/mod.rs","rust/loopflow/src/work/wave/config.rs","rust/loopflow/src/work/wave/context.rs","rust/loopflow/tests/dto_fixtures.rs","rust/loopflow/tests/flow_tests.rs","rust/loopflow/tests/global_commands.rs","rust/loopflow/tests/pr_tests.rs","rust/loopflow/tests/repository_team_matrix.rs"]},{"sha":"632b67ec7e98be40fd0b9720b513165f90ef2bef","title":"Recover failed release CI and preserve cron failures (#1311)","files":[".lf/flows/release-run.yaml","python/tests/test_release_automation.py","release/CRON_HOST.md","release/README.md","rust/loopflow/src/lf/commands/flow.rs","rust/loopflow/src/lf/commands/ops/mod.rs","rust/loopflow/src/ops/pr.rs","rust/loopflow/src/ops/pr_landing.rs","rust/loopflow/src/ops/release.rs","rust/loopflow/tests/flow_tests.rs","rust/loopflow/tests/release_tests.rs","scripts/test_task_installation.py","swift/LoopflowTests/ActiveRunsObservationTests.swift","wave/infrastructure/MEMORY.md","wave/infrastructure/release/MEMORY.md"]}],"merged_prs":[{"number":1307,"title":"Unify account auth, remember browser profiles, and retain usage evidence","body":"Account login and inspection were spread across separate commands, Claude's normal hyperlink output could time out before opening a browser, and successful usage responses were discarded. This change provides one `lf auth` surface, captures the provider's native browser handoff, and retains subscription observations for later offline inspection.\n\n<!-- loopflow:task-pr-context:start -->\n> [!NOTE]\n> **Task:** [Make account login, usage, and auth output clear and reliable · LOO-320](https://linear.app/loopflow/issue/LOO-320/make-account-login-usage-and-auth-output-clear-and-reliable)\n> **PR lifecycle:** Merging PR 1 completes the Task.\n<!-- loopflow:task-pr-context:end -->\n\n## What changes\n\n- Six auth leaves replace the old account/profile/access commands and top-level routing commands. Reusable Chrome profiles remain, with independent remembered choices for managed accounts and local services such as Linear.\n- Native callback completion and explicit hidden manual input replace Chrome page/clipboard scraping. New managed accounts are staged and identity-checked before registration.\n- Cached text and JSON distinguish managed credentials, local tokens and uninspected forwarding. Missing credentials stay visible; named windows retain their source, age and reset time. Verification writes returned windows atomically and preserves routing/cooldown.\n- Account and route listings show IDs beside logins. Headless Runs record the account actually selected per attempt before a provider Session ID exists.\n- The forward migration preserves populated account/profile/route history. Published Rust API changes and their replacements are documented in [Rust API migration](https://github.com/loopflowstudio/loopflow/blob/jack-heart/make-account-login-usage-and/docs/subscriptions.md#rust-api-migration); `wait_for_auth` exposes the existing per-attempt completion result to crate callers.\n\n## Limits retained at approval\n\nJack Heart approved the delivered scope and directed queue/landing. Four live checks remain unproven: browser login without pasting a code, first-time managed connection, remembered Linear profile targeting, and real Claude/Codex usage windows. The configured Claude probe returned `invalid_grant`; its usage decoder fixture remains synthetic. PTY/manual-fallback and installed acceptance are not established by fixture tests.\n\nCross-account Session continuation, native credential refresh coordination and remaining-headroom ranking are outside this delivery. The copied-Home demo also retained a pre-migration `status --details` failure and a route/status disagreement between stored connected evidence and an absent credential. [Infrastructure memory](https://github.com/loopflowstudio/loopflow/blob/jack-heart/make-account-login-usage-and/wave/infrastructure/MEMORY.md#account-auth-consolidation-loo-320-branch-evidence-2026-09-27) preserves these decisions and links to the original evidence.\n\n## Checks\n\nThe changed-aware gate passed architecture, 250 Python tests, 2,127 Rust tests (nine skipped) and 78 website checks (three skipped). Rust ran with materialized migrations in disposable storage. Formatting, Clippy with warnings denied, migration history, Ruff and shell syntax passed. Fresh-Home `runs`, `usage` and `doctor` JSON checks passed; doctor retained empty-history/freshness warnings.\n\nOne telemetry fixture required termination of its verified stalled SSH fetch child; it then passed with freshness unavailable. This is an intervened local result, not proof of unattended fetch completion. Provider, browser, broker and account effects are simulated; they do not establish the four live checks above. Swift, app/UI and slow end-to-end suites remain with CI. No candidate command opened the installed Home.\n\n## Try it\n\nAfter ordinary delivery, run `lf auth status`, then `lf auth status --details` to inspect account IDs, cached window ages and remembered browser bindings. Use `lf auth status codex --verify` for an intended account set, then plain status to read its retained observations offline. These are suggested steps; successful live verif","files":[],"additions":4943,"deletions":2022,"changed_files":44,"merge_commit":"280670217b0da8f2a541b655b9965c79124a1660"},{"number":1308,"title":"Keep branch builds on private data and installed Tasks on their owning runtime","body":"Running a branch build could expose installed Task history to development migrations and inherited execution context. Branch builds now keep private data, while managed Task launches and continuation use the selected installation’s executable and database together.\n\n<!-- loopflow:task-pr-context:start -->\n> [!NOTE]\n> **Task:** [A branch build never migrates a Home that a release owns · LOO-321](https://linear.app/loopflow/issue/LOO-321/a-branch-build-never-migrates-a-home-that-a-release-owns)\n> **PR lifecycle:** Merging PR 1 completes the Task.\n<!-- loopflow:task-pr-context:end -->\n\n## What changes\n\n- Seed installation-owned data into a source-specific directory once, preserving subsequent private writes and clearing inherited execution authority. Home identities and placement remain intact.\n- Route managed Task operations before preparation, checkpoints or worker claims. Return installed Task state and consume installed review readiness without transferring branch-only identities or feedback.\n- Make `lf task run` start or continue saved work; reserve `task restart` for replacing its invocation. Rename preparation to `task checkout`, which also restores missing checkouts from retained history and works from dirty checkouts.\n- Connect Wave chat automatically when opened. Remove Wave lifecycle and Task/Wave enablement controls across the CLI, app and DTOs. Move readers to `catalog`, `wave list`, `wave status`, `wave probe` and `pr checks`, without compatibility aliases.\n- Block installation changes from Task execution. Incompatible-database errors retain migration evidence and recommend recovery pairs only after verifying their artifacts and exact database compatibility.\n\n## Limits\n\nBranch and installed databases do not synchronize; branch status can therefore differ from a managed operation’s returned state. Database isolation does not isolate provider mutations or shared checkout edits. Remote placement remains supported, but remote chat transport is not added to the app.\n\n## Checks\n\nAdds a required disposable Linux installation job covering continuation, review completion, store protection and recovery. The committed proof ledger records four passing installation scenarios plus focused Rust/Swift and static checks; these were not rerun for this description. GitHub and chat providers are simulated, and review Runs are prepared without launching a provider. Live installed-worker acceptance remains unproven.\n\n## Try it\n\nSuggested walkthrough, not performed for this description: open a locally placed Wave’s chat in the app or with `lf chat --follow -w <wave>`. Its conversation should connect automatically without a separate start action.","files":[],"additions":4272,"deletions":2910,"changed_files":167,"merge_commit":"418e52ba652c4054879da67851f18d23e6b64a62"},{"number":1311,"title":"Recover failed release CI and preserve cron failures","body":"Scheduled releases now hand failed required checks to the existing landing repair supervisor, and cron receives the release operation's actual exit status. A locally reproduced blocking Swift fixture join is replaced with bounded asynchronous exit observation.\n\nRelease retains version-metadata rebuilding when main advances and preserves blocked repair checkouts. The scheduled release target is a deterministic operation Flow, selected before the same-named skill. GitHub's temporary no-checks response after a push remains pending. Cold installation-proof image downloads have a network deadline separate from container creation.\n\nIncident findings live at `wave/infrastructure/release/MEMORY.md`. Addresses [release recovery · LOO-328](https://linear.app/loopflow/issue/LOO-328) and the Swift hang portion of LOO-326; its other faults remain open. The local sample proves the cleanup defect; the original hosted job retained no stack.\n\nChecks: 338 Swift tests; 57 release tests including simulated failed-check repair before tagging; 14 landing tests; 27 PR tests including the observed no-checks response; 10 Python release automation tests; CLI Flow failure propagation and cron precedence. All four disposable Linux installation proofs passed. Cargo fmt, all-target Clippy and scoped Ruff pass. Rebased onto #1308. Hosted Swift execution passed on an earlier head; final-head CI and live publication remain the delivery gates.","files":[],"additions":436,"deletions":36,"changed_files":15,"merge_commit":"632b67ec7e98be40fd0b9720b513165f90ef2bef"}],"decisions":null,"previous_release_notes":"# v0.12.23\n\n<!-- loopflow:release-notes=narrative;gate=safe -->\n\nv0.12.23 makes unattended Tasks easier to steer and recover: agent choices persist, failed decisions expose their blockers, and stalled work becomes visible. Planning moves into Task, Wave, and repository commands, with retryable deletion that preserves historical evidence. Release retries can also reuse a version after its earlier release PR was withdrawn.\n\n## Keep Task choices through execution and recovery\n\nA Task's selected agent now survives launch, resume, restart, and review, overriding skill defaults without changing the configured default. The implementation loop is shorter, and CLI and desktop show blocked or stalled execution with recovery guidance.\n\n- Failed decisions retain their Run and open a keyed unblock Session instead of leaving the Task looking ready.\n- Five minutes without events or sampled body/tool CPU progress shows **Stalled**. Missing or mismatched samples remain **Unknown**; observing a stall does not authorize termination.\n- The `pursue` Flow runs implement → compress → review-slice → loop-decide. Compress edits code; review-slice reports replacement evidence and convergence blockers. Concept review remains interactive, and shipping removes the redundant task-gate wrapper.\n\n## Manage planning and deletion through one command family\n\nTask creation, editing, comments, and completion now live under `lf task`. Deletion handles both registered and planning-only Tasks, so removing an issue no longer requires separate Linear and local actions.\n\n- Use `lf task delete ISSUE` to delete a Task. Confirmed deletion removes it from current planning views while preserving completed outcomes, timestamps, authored files, and retained PRs. Explicit `lf task status ISSUE` keeps historical lookup available.\n- Saved issue identity and deletion confirmation let retries survive planning refresh and chapter replacement. Missing provider data never counts as confirmed deletion. Chapter rotation now sends untouched backlog to Linear's native trash.\n- Planning-only creation requires no checkout or execution credentials. `create --run` validates execution before filing the issue and reuses that issue on retry.\n- Connection, sync, and placement move to `lf wave`; provider administration moves to `lf repo`; planning diagnostics use `lf doctor --planning`.\n- Checkout Task identity comes from the checked-out branch, and completion evidence survives provider writeback retries.\n\n## Operational notes\n\n- **Command migration:** `pm`, `work`, and superseded Task commands are removed without aliases. Update scripts to the Task, Wave, repository, and doctor commands above; desktop callers, bundled skills, and documentation have been updated.\n- Task deletion does not certify process termination or complete Session/Run cleanup. Recorded Runs retain their attribution.\n- `lf release run` ignores release PRs closed without merging when finding a version's PR. A withdrawn PR no longer forces skipping that version; open and merged PRs still participate in lookup.\n- The Swift CI test step now times out after 20 minutes, allowing a hung step to fail and be rerun. The intermittent observation-cancellation test hang itself remains unfixed.\n- Only free disk space gates builds. Oversized sibling checkouts warn; the current checkout cleans its own oversized disposable build roots.\n- Recorded checks cover the affected Task suites, deletion and retry behavior, and all 41 release-module tests. Configured Claude launch/resume, a live five-minute stall, rendered Task states, installed deletion acceptance, and end-to-end release retry remain unverified in the supplied evidence. The final decision-policy revision also lacks live proof; earlier policy evidence used simulated planning state and synthetic feedback.\n\n## Small changes\n\n- Ruff is updated from 0.16.3 to 0.16.4.","source_limits":{"context_bytes":131072,"commits":256,"merged_prs":200,"files_per_change":100,"area_scopes":32,"name_bytes":256,"title_bytes":300,"path_bytes":512,"pr_body_bytes":4096,"decisions_bytes":16384,"previous_release_notes_bytes":16384,"release_notes_bytes":61440},"omissions":{"commits":0,"merged_prs":0,"commit_files":67,"pr_files":0,"area_scopes":0,"text_bytes":209,"decisions_bytes":0,"previous_release_notes_bytes":0}}